tus="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAKEFUDA, AKIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MASUDA, NORIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAZAKI, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WADA, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, TOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Novel isoquinoline derivatives represented by general formula (I) or salts thereof which have an If current inhibitory effect without any serious side effects such as convulsion; and drugs, in particular, cardiac rate lowering agents containing these compounds as the active ingredient. Namely, dialkoxy-1,2,3,4-tetrahydroquinoline-2-carbonylpiperidino-3,4-dialkoxypropananilide derivatives, etc. which have an If current inhibitory effect and are useful, as cardiac rate lowering agents, particularly in preventing ischemic heart diseases such as precordial anxiety (thoracic precordial anxiety) and myocardial infarct, and circulatory diseases such as congestive heart failure and arrhythmia (supraventricular arrhythmia, etc.).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne des dérivés d'isoquinoline représentés par la formule générale (I) ou leurs sels. Ces composés ont une action inhibitrice sur le courant If, sans effets secondaires sérieux du type convulsions. L'invention concerne également des médicaments, en particulier des abaisseurs de rythme cardiaque renfermant ces composés comme principe actif. Il s'agit en l'occurrence des dérivés de dialkoxy-1,2,3,4-tétrahydroquinoline-2carbonylpiperidino-3,4-dialkoxypropananilide, etc. qui ont une activité inhibitrice sur le courant If et qui conviennent comme abaisseurs de rythme cardiaque, en particulier pour la prévention des cardiopathies ischémiques telles que l'anxiété thoracique précordiale) et l'infarctus du myocarde ainsi que les troubles circulatoires tels que l'insuffisance cardiaque globale et l'arythmie (arythmie supraventriculaire, etc.).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>